    "result_text": "There is only one test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires the created/returned owner to expose `displayName` formatted as `LastName, FirstName`. I made two small, cohesive changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates the `OwnerDto` with a `displayName` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 annotated the existing `toOwnerDto` method with a single MapStruct expression mapping that computes the value from the stored names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   ```\n\nThis keeps structural impact minimal: the logic lives in the small `OwnerMapper` (low `WMC_other`), the changed method has CC 1 with one changed line, and I avoided touching the large `Owner`/`Person` domain classes or any controller. The `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName` test and the full suite pass.",
